From 38875bbcd896331ca86d6e87de2945ed352e25fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:52:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(import): give the STEP face evaluation cap measured
 headroom; a finer pass over a continuous face keeps the coarser mesh

#1546's per-face evaluation cap (25 M) refused healthy models: 10208.STEP
at the 60 M facet budget was refused on face #1073, which converges at
28.07 M evaluations, and 32050.STEP used 92 % of the cap at the default
budget.

- FACE_EVAL_CAP is 150 M: 5.3x the heaviest healthy face measured, and a
  runaway face still ends in 10-15 s in release.
- A refinement pass that trips the cap on a face proven continuous
  (step_continuity: analytic, or a B-spline/NURBS with interior knot
  multiplicity <= degree, finite points and positive weights, divided
  only inside its own parameter range) keeps the coarser mesh at its own
  chord, as a pass over the facet budget does. Any other trip still
  refuses by name; the #1536 smear (and sc_logo.step's face #836, whose
  division range ran to u = -2e51) still refuse.
- A continuous face refused on its first pass is no longer called
  discontinuous.
- step_guard's tests move to step_guard_tests.rs (400-line law).

Fixes #1568

